& [DevelopmentNeed]
  + use one reusable WSL Cargo target rather than a new target for every checkpoint
  + inspect Windows system-volume free space before expensive verification
  + default to a read-only machine-readable plan
  + execute only when explicitly selected
  + serialize Cargo build jobs and Rust test threads for the complete regression lane
  + refuse execution below a declared free-space threshold
  + never delete caches automatically
  + never contact a remote host or write into OneDrive
  + leave cleanup as a separately inspected and explicitly selected operation

& [SelectedPrototype]
  + one PowerShell entry point composes preflight and either workspace tests or warnings-denied Clippy inside one named WSL distribution
  + one offline contract test proves plan shape closed action selection threshold refusal and absence of remote or destructive operations
  + this is development-machine operational policy not product runtime authority
